    "done_when": "Section 2's default scope in reckon/crew/dispatch.py grants the node's own fragment and figure directory to every role, so a verifier role, meaning review and read-only investigate, receives repository write paths it must not have. After this node, only roles that land work in the tree receive the default fragment path fragment path under docs/evidence/fragments/ and the matching figure directory under docs/figures/. A verifier role's write scope carries none of them. The set of landing roles is read from where dispatch already decides which roles are repository-writing, not listed a second time.\n\ntests/test_role_write_scope.py has two tests that fail at main 29af302f:\n- test_an_implement_role_receives_the_landing_paths_in_its_write_scope\n- test_an_implement_role_on_the_local_lane_still_receives_the_landing_paths\nThey assert the shared landing paths that section 2 replaced. Reconcile both with section 2's rule: an implement role receives its own fragment and figure paths, and no shared plan or archive path. Keep each test's intent. Add a case asserting that a review role and a read-only investigate role receive neither path.\n\ntests/test_role_write_scope.py passes at exit 0. The manifest writes baseline_suite and after_suite over that file and tests/test_crew.py, each as one line of armed JSON: revision, command with no placeholder, exit_status, completed, failure_count, failure_ids, log_path. Those two ids are fixed at head, and no other id is added. Every gate log opens with one line naming its revision, tree and command. The declared negative control is applied and observed to fail, and its log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED id.",
